content.text:
The people page now shows a "Grand influence" figure: everyone's influence added together. Anyone whose influence is "n/a" is left out of the sum. `bin/e2e` passes, including the check that earlier test data still seeds and reads back correctly.

I only changed the front end, in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`. The server already works out each person's influence, so no data or server changes were needed. I added:
- a `grandInfluence` value, calculated the same way as the existing totals like "Grand flow";
- a "Grand influence" line in the summary under "Grand flow", tagged `rollup-grand-influence`;
- a line in the file's header comments describing the new figure.

With the test's data the page shows 525. Ada, Ben, Cam and Dot have influence 60, 120, 300 and 45. Eli is skipped because a missing alpha makes his influence "n/a".

